PUPPET TECHNIQUE MANUAL -- SUNAGAKURE PUPPET BRIGADE

The Puppet Technique (Kugutsu no Jutsu) is the pride of the Hidden Sand. The
user extends threads of chakra from the fingertips to animate a constructed
puppet at range, turning a lifeless body of wood and steel into a lethal
combatant while the master remains beyond reach.

Fundamentals:
1. Thread control -- one chakra string per finger for a novice; masters such
   as those of the Brigade command hundreds of threads and multiple puppets.
2. Concealed armament -- puppets house hidden blades, poison senbon launchers,
   flamethrowers, and dispersal mechanisms. Every joint may hide a weapon.
3. Poison doctrine -- Sunagakure puppets are traditionally coated or loaded
   with fast-acting poisons brewed by the Poison Division; a single graze can
   decide a battle.

The finest recorded puppeteers include Chiyo the Honored Grandmother, her
grandson Sasori (defected), and Kankuro of the Sand Siblings, current field
exemplar. Advanced study of human puppets is restricted to sealed manuals.
